for more than two decades the russian  president has been cultivating a strong  man image  he's a judo master who rides horses  swims in a siberian river and scores  goals in hockey against world champions  but in the past few months that image  has been challenged  recent footage of the 69 year old leader  showed him coughing puffy faced or  walking with a stiff right arm feeling  speculation and questions from the media  about his health after two years of  pandemic isolation  in late july intelligence officers  shared their assessments there are lots  of rumors and as far as we can tell he's  entirely too healthy and the kremlin has  repeatedly said he's doing well  so amid the war in ukraine here's why  putin's every public appearance is being  so closely scrutinized  first consider that we're getting very  little information from russia on the  president's well-being good afternoon  everybody unlike the white house that  shares regular health updates for u.s  leaders president biden is currently  experiencing mild symptoms the kremlin  is very tight-lipped on the matter  so videos of a seemingly tired putin  sitting at the victory day parade or  holding the table with both hands during  this televised update about the war in  ukraine  prompted comments by officials and news  outlets around the world about his  fitness  a top ukrainian official told a tv  channel that the russian leader was sick  a newsweek report claiming that american  spies believed putin had been treated  for cancer was widely covered  so journalists have been asking russian  officials about it  yesterday  the wall street journal couldn't  independently confirm those reports and  the leader of a european country told us  he believed putin was healthy still  observers noticed that when putin landed  in tehran he seemed to walk stiffly with  his right arm hanging unnaturally  he also repeatedly coughed and cleared  his throat during and after this trip so  much so that he spoke about it himself  it's obviously hard to draw any  conclusion from this type of footage but  it puts putin's health in the spotlight  even making it a talking point at a  major security forum and prompting  western intelligence chiefs to weigh in  there's no evidence that uh putin is uh  is suffering from serious ill health  what footage from the past couple of  years does show clearly is that the  russian leader appears to take his  physical well-being seriously that's  what these extremely long meeting tables  suggest  in the early days of the pandemic putin  went into isolation in his residence  outside moscow  during two years he mostly communicated  with the outside world via video calls  like most leaders around the world  but even after he started attending more  in-person events during russia's war  with ukraine most of the time the public  has been kept at a distance  the same goes for officials and world  leaders who've often been seated far  away from him  this 16 feet long table was seen several  times during putin's meeting with  france's emanuel macron and germany's  olaf schultz among others the kremlin  said it was keeping in place all the  safety measures to protect the president  from the coronavirus  the health of world leaders is always a  matter of public concern false reports  recently claimed that the ukrainian  president was in intensive care for  example  [Applause]  but for russia heightened scrutiny of  putin's health also brings questions  about how the country would be governed  without its authoritative leader at a  time when he's at the center of global  politics over the invasion of ukraine  for decades moscow has worked hard to  create an aura around one man as the  country's main decision maker who's  believed to directly approve almost all  executive government decisions  the kremlin said that putin's  decision-making powers are limited by  the russian constitution and the  president's spokesman has previously  said moscow isn't looking for a  successor and that means any contingency  plan will likely remain a closely held  secret
 

